WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:39.500
We know that the snake is utilized conceptually
and metaphorically as representation of transformation,

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:43.930
right because the snake is something that
can shed its skin and be reborn.

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:48.710
We know that a snake is something that’s
innately attractive and terrifying to human

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:54.640
beings and other primates so that if you come
across a snake, you’re likely to be at least

00:00:54.640 --> 00:01:00.000
startled, if not horrified by it but also
attracted to it in a way that is underneath

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.830
your voluntary consciousness,
right, because snakes attract orienting reflexes

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:08.920
and they activate the systems underneath your
consciousness that actually govern the structure

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:10.910
of that consciousness.

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:16.930
We know that the snake can be well represented
as well as internal chaos so imagine this.

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:22.630
Imagine that it’s not unreasonable for a
self-conscious mind searching for a mode of

00:01:22.630 --> 00:01:27.960
self-representation to remark on the parallels
between the structure of the snake and the

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:33.220
spine and the brain given that a snake is
essentially a spine with a brain and then

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:39.280
imagine as well that the most archaic aspects
of our nervous system, those that govern novelty

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:44.380
and orienting and anxiety responses or in
fact precisely those that were described by

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:50.890
McLean as nested inside the reptilian brain
and then imagine along with the Hindu Yogis

00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:56.420
that the purpose of Kundalini Yoga is to activate
the circuitry that’s associated with that

00:01:56.420 --> 00:02:02.780
snake so-to-speak, to produce a permanent
state of alert wakefulness that’s associated

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:08.580
with consciousness.

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:09.880
So imagine this.

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:16.770
Imagine an animal like, like a zebra, grazing
mindlessly in the herd with no consciousness

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:17.770
whatsoever.

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:23.310
And then imagine its relatively undeveloped
cortical structures activated suddenly by

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:27.170
the movement of a lion off in the perimeter.

00:02:27.170 --> 00:02:31.350
And then imagine for that brief
moment, that that zebra’s actually conscious,

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:34.900
a state that requires a tremendous amount
of energy and difficult to maintain,

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:41.330
but because the threat and the uncertainty
manifests itself within the Zebra’s mode

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:44.040
of consciousness it wakes momentarily.

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:49.030
And then imagine that human beings are like
that zebra, always.

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:53.540
Because we’ve become so conscious, because
we note that the unknown is around us all

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:57.610
the time, even when we think we’re safe,
we’re never safe.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:01.700
Imagine that the reason we’re so conscious
is because as a consequence of our discovery

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:07.470
of the possibility of our own mortality, all
this underlying circuitry that in other animals

00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:12.500
is only apparent when they’re startled or
afraid or interested or curious.

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:15.620
In human beings it’s on all the time and
that’s what makes us conscious

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:21.480
and the reason for that is because we developed
enough cortical elaboration to note that we’re

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:24.240
always threatened by everything that’s around
us.

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:27.500
And then imagine that – well that’s pretty
awful isn’t it?

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:32.700
because it’s at the basis of all our innate
existential terror – but then imagine as

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:38.960
well that without that terror pushing us forward
and and our constant reference to the dangerous

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:43.890
aspect of the unknown, we would have never
been motivated to produce the kind of societies

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:51.150
that we’ve produced which are essentially
very remarkably elaborated devices that enable

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:56.920
us to find some protection from that unknown
and to manipulate it effectively.

00:03:56.920 --> 00:04:02.170
And then remembering that story, we’ll return
to Genesis.

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:10.210
Jung says the snake was regarded by early
Gnostic Christians as a kind of deity whose

00:04:10.210 --> 00:04:14.980
faculties were more developed and advanced
than the original Deity that actually structured

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:15.980
the world,

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:20.680
the idea there being that the world initially
was a pretty abysmal place.

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:22.169
Everyone wasn’t conscious.

00:04:22.169 --> 00:04:27.979
We all existed at the level of the animal
and then the snake came along and said, “wake

00:04:27.979 --> 00:04:29.600
up, wake up”.

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:36.220
And the movement from that state of unselfconsciousness
paradise to this profane state of awakening

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:42.350
can be regarded not so much as a descent but
as an ascent of sorts even though a painful

00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:43.650
one.

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:51.340
And then you have Goethe’s commentary from
Mephistopheles, his representation of Satan

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:54.110
and his capacity for temptation who says:

00:04:54.110 --> 00:04:59.979
"follow the adage of my cousin snake/ from
Dreams of Godlike knowledge you will wake

00:04:59.979 --> 00:05:03.349
/ to fear in which your very soul shall quake."

00:05:03.349 --> 00:05:12.699
A statement associateing the human tendency
to attribute to all revolutionary sources

00:05:12.699 --> 00:05:17.240
of new information a kind of demonic being.

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:20.360
And then you have the problem of the woman.

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:25.570
Now we know that within the context of the
Judeo-Christian tradition women have unduly

00:05:25.570 --> 00:05:32.729
suffered for their role in tempting humanity
in the embodied form of Adam towards higher

00:05:32.729 --> 00:05:36.169
order self consciousness
and then you think well, let’s just take

00:05:36.169 --> 00:05:41.289
a look at how human beings and their mating
relationships differ from those of other animals

00:05:41.289 --> 00:05:45.009
like chimpanzees to whom we are very closely
genetically related.

00:05:45.009 --> 00:05:49.469
And if you look at the mating strategies of
female chimpanzees you see that they really

00:05:49.469 --> 00:05:52.770
don’t care who they sleep with, so to speak.

00:05:52.770 --> 00:05:54.659
Any old chimpanzee will do.

00:05:54.659 --> 00:05:59.879
Now, the less dominant male chimps tend to
be chased away by the more dominant male chimps

00:05:59.879 --> 00:06:04.520
but if a female and less dominant chimp can
get the hell away from the watchful gaze of

00:06:04.520 --> 00:06:07.860
the dominants already, they’re perfectly
happy to mate.

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:10.110
Human females are not like that.

00:06:10.110 --> 00:06:12.280
They’re selective maters.

00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:17.039
And there’s a tremendous body of evolutionary
psychological information that suggests that

00:06:17.039 --> 00:06:24.870
although both genders value intelligence and
physical appearance, females value the ability

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:32.610
to attain dominance hierarchy status in men
far more than men admire the ability to attain

00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:34.129
dominant status in women.

00:06:34.129 --> 00:06:39.529
which is to say that men don’t care what
a woman has with regards to potential for

00:06:39.529 --> 00:06:44.979
attaining status, whereas with women it’s
one of the strong determinants of mating preference.

00:06:44.979 --> 00:06:49.939
So then let’s say look we don’t know why
the hell our cortexes expanded so rapidly

00:06:49.939 --> 00:06:52.669
somewhere between five and three million years
ago.

00:06:52.669 --> 00:06:55.120
Let’s offer this as a hypothesis.

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:59.069
The women started to get choosy and because
they were so damned complicated the whole

00:06:59.069 --> 00:07:05.960
human species had to exaggerate its cortical
growth prior to any even use for that cortical

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:10.879
growth just so that the men had an even hand
in the competition, right.

00:07:10.879 --> 00:07:16.529
So women put tremendous selection pressure
on the human being to develop tremendous,

00:07:16.529 --> 00:07:18.490
tremendous cortical expansion.

00:07:18.490 --> 00:07:23.830
Now, we already know that from the mythological
perspective that women are frequently cast

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:30.349
into the same conceptual domain - the temptress
domain - as the benevolent aspect of the unknown

00:07:30.349 --> 00:07:34.979
and we know as well from representations of
hero mythology that it is the individual who

00:07:34.979 --> 00:07:40.259
goes out to confront chaos whose most likely
to free from the dragon not only treasure

00:07:40.259 --> 00:07:46.039
but a virgin say in the case of mythological
representations like say George and the Dragon.

00:07:46.039 --> 00:07:53.520
So then we close with the notion of voluntarism
and in the Old Testament in Genesis, there’s

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:58.470
now there’s this notion that not only did
people become self-conscious because they

00:07:58.470 --> 00:08:01.270
did something but they did this voluntarily
right?

00:08:01.270 --> 00:08:07.860
They they they made this decision on their
own.

00:08:07.860 --> 00:08:16.710
So Milton puts words into God’s mouth and
says, "So will fall/ He and his faithless

00:08:16.710 --> 00:08:19.080
progeny: whose fault?

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:20.250
/ Whose but his own?

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:25.909
/ ingrate, he had of me/ All he could have;
I made him just and right,/ sufficient to

00:08:25.909 --> 00:08:28.990
have stood, though free to fall.”

00:08:28.990 --> 00:08:34.149
and then you think if you think well maybe
the notion of the heritable sin of Adam characterizing

00:08:34.149 --> 00:08:38.820
human beings and their fallen existential
condition isn’t just the black-hearted ravings

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:41.470
of fundamentalist southern Baptist lunatics.

00:08:41.470 --> 00:08:42.470
Right?

00:08:42.470 --> 00:08:44.030
There’s something to this.

00:08:44.030 --> 00:08:48.529
Human beings are the only creatures that seem
to live at odds with their own experience

00:08:48.529 --> 00:08:53.460
and it’s not so unreasonable to suppose
that it’s our dawning capacity for self

00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:57.430
consciousness that put us in that uncomfortable
position.

00:08:57.430 --> 00:09:02.010
So why do I associate the eating of the apple
with self consciousness?

00:09:02.010 --> 00:09:05.020
Well, it’s because that’s how the story
lays itself out.

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:09.410
You have the collateral evidence of the Buddhist
story of enlightenment, right?

00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:10.730
His contact with death.

00:09:10.730 --> 00:09:17.790
You have multiple medie, medieval representations
of Eve offering to animal, to Adam not an

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:19.990
apple but a skull.

00:09:19.990 --> 00:09:24.160
You have multiple representations of the tree
of the knowledge of good and evil in the medieval

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:28.770
iconography as not containing apples but containing
skulls.

00:09:28.770 --> 00:09:34.440
And you have the the statements that are within
the context of Genesis itself.

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:39.060
"And the eyes of both of them were opened.

00:09:39.060 --> 00:09:40.780
And they knew that they were naked.

00:09:40.780 --> 00:09:44.080
And they sewed fig leaves together and made
themselves aprons.

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:48.070
Well, there’s a lot of information packed
into those two lines, right?

00:09:48.070 --> 00:09:49.750
What does it mean to have your eyes open?

00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:52.670
Well half your brain is visual cortex.

00:09:52.670 --> 00:10:00.650
it’s not unreasonable to presume that that
means that quick, a quick magnification of

00:10:00.650 --> 00:10:01.650
consciousness.

00:10:01.650 --> 00:10:02.650
You’re conscious during the day.

00:10:02.650 --> 00:10:03.740
That’s when your eyes are open.

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:05.900
But what happens when your eyes are open?

00:10:05.900 --> 00:10:07.230
Well, you know you’re naked.

00:10:07.230 --> 00:10:08.370
Well what does that mean?

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:13.040
Well, you know you’re vulnerable, right
to social comment, to social judgment, to

00:10:13.040 --> 00:10:17.210
dominance, hierarchy, status manoeuvering
and to all the terrible things that the unknown

00:10:17.210 --> 00:10:20.560
world can can heap upon you.

00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:22.290
And so then what do you do?

00:10:22.290 --> 00:10:23.870
Well you create culture.

00:10:23.870 --> 00:10:24.870
Right?

00:10:24.870 --> 00:10:26.370
And that’s what this little sentence said.

00:10:26.370 --> 00:10:29.650
"And they sewed fig leaves together and made
themselves aprons."

00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:39.180
That’s a pretty eventful sequence all crammed
up in two little sentences.

00:10:39.180 --> 00:10:40.210
So then what happens?

00:10:40.210 --> 00:10:43.500
Ah I think it’s extremely interesting.

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:47.560
So before Adam and Eve figure out that they’re
naked, they’re cruising around the garden

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:49.550
having a fine time doing whatever they want.

00:10:49.550 --> 00:10:51.510
They don’t take any thought for the future,
right?

00:10:51.510 --> 00:10:53.330
They don’t have a pre frontal cortex.

00:10:53.330 --> 00:11:00.470
They’re living in a, in a paradox-less environment
like an animal lives.

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:03.570
Well what happens after they become self conscious?

00:11:03.570 --> 00:11:07.500
Well, prior to this Adam’s walking around
with God right?

00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:08.620
And you think about what that means.

00:11:08.620 --> 00:11:10.490
Does it mean something like this?

00:11:10.490 --> 00:11:13.340
An animal isn’t in the world of good and
evil.

00:11:13.340 --> 00:11:16.520
An animal like Nietzsche points out is beyond
good and evil, right?

00:11:16.520 --> 00:11:22.750
Enraptured in te, entirely by the actions
of automatic instinct, governed by processes

00:11:22.750 --> 00:11:25.030
that are completely transcendent.

00:11:25.030 --> 00:11:27.630
The animal’s nothing but a force of nature.

00:11:27.630 --> 00:11:30.341
There’s no opposition between the animal
and the world.

00:11:30.341 --> 00:11:33.030
The animal is the world.

00:11:33.030 --> 00:11:38.680
And just as in the case of the animal prior
to the eating of the apple, Adam walks around

00:11:38.680 --> 00:11:40.050
the garden with God.

00:11:40.050 --> 00:11:47.420
There’s no discontinuity between Him and
the, and the transcendent world as such but

00:11:47.420 --> 00:11:51.540
as soon as he becomes naked, he hides.

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:52.710
Well why?

00:11:52.710 --> 00:11:54.170
Well that doesn’t need to be answered.

00:11:54.170 --> 00:11:56.290
All you have to do is think about it.

00:11:56.290 --> 00:11:58.990
Why would you hide if you know you’re naked?

00:11:58.990 --> 00:12:00.490
Well, it’s simple.

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:03.100
You hide because you think you can get hurt.

00:12:03.100 --> 00:12:09.710
You think that whatever you are is so vulnerable
that if it shows itself to the transcendent

00:12:09.710 --> 00:12:15.180
to others, to the natural road that something
terrible will happen and then you think well

00:12:15.180 --> 00:12:18.630
that’s a pretty logical pre-supposition
right?

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:22.890
Look at us.

00:12:22.890 --> 00:12:30.060
So God comes cruising around the garden after
Adam and Eve eat the apple in the cool of

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:35.230
the day, and Adam and Eve hide themselves
among the trees of the garden.

00:12:35.230 --> 00:12:40.370
And God says, hey Adam hey, where are you?

00:12:40.370 --> 00:12:47.330
And Adam says, “I heard your voice and I
was afraid because I was naked and I hid myself”.

00:12:47.330 --> 00:12:54.240
And that story has bottomless depth because
it means something like this.

00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:58.500
At the beginning of Genesis, there’s this
notion that there is a transcendent relationship

00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:00.550
between the individual and God, right?

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:03.780
The identity of logos and the individual right?

00:13:03.780 --> 00:13:10.300
A notion by the way that our entire idea of
intrinsic human right is predicated on as

00:13:10.300 --> 00:13:12.810
we’ve been at some pains to demonstrate.

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:20.590
A relationship between the limited and the
limitless eradicated by the dawn of self-consciousness.

00:13:20.590 --> 00:13:21.650
Well what does that mean?

00:13:21.650 --> 00:13:25.090
Well, let’s say you have a destiny just
for the sake of argument.

00:13:25.090 --> 00:13:26.090
Right?

00:13:26.090 --> 00:13:30.700
Because you are a being with a tremendous
history and an unbelievable potential.

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:33.620
So let’s say you have a destiny, just for
the sake of argument.

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:37.670
What would cause you to hide from that destiny?

00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:44.000
Well, obviously your own reflection’s on
your mortal vulnerability, right?

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:53.110
How could I be characterized by any transcendent
power whatsoever when I’m susceptible to

00:13:53.110 --> 00:13:54.900
social alienation, right?

00:13:54.900 --> 00:14:01.400
When I have this body which is capable of
terrifying degeneration that will eventually

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:04.840
decay into old age and that is bounded by
death.

00:14:04.840 --> 00:14:11.650
How could I be good for anything which is
precisely what this little story says.

00:14:11.650 --> 00:14:16.770
And so God figures out that Adam and Eve at
the fruit and that’s pretty decisive move

00:14:16.770 --> 00:14:19.950
because once you wake up, sorry, you’re
awake.

00:14:19.950 --> 00:14:24.060
And he says, and this is not an injunction
by the way.

00:14:24.060 --> 00:14:25.270
This is the description.

00:14:25.270 --> 00:14:27.560
All right, you’ve done it now.

00:14:27.560 --> 00:14:32.090
“And to the woman he says, I will greatly
multiply thy sorrow and thy conception.

00:14:32.090 --> 00:14:34.450
In sorry shalt thou bring forth children."

00:14:34.450 --> 00:14:35.450
Why?

00:14:35.450 --> 00:14:36.450
Why?

00:14:36.450 --> 00:14:41.190
Well, we have a big cortex, right?

00:14:41.190 --> 00:14:42.190
Really big.

00:14:42.190 --> 00:14:47.020
It grew fast and what that meant is that there
was an evolutionary arms race between skull

00:14:47.020 --> 00:14:54.250
size, date of birth, and pelvic diameter girth.

00:14:54.250 --> 00:14:59.000
The wider the pelvis, the less effectively
you can walk.

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:01.860
The larger the skull, the bigger the brain.

00:15:01.860 --> 00:15:05.540
The younger the baby, the more dependent and
vulnerable.

00:15:05.540 --> 00:15:08.290
So what do we have in the case of human beings?

00:15:08.290 --> 00:15:13.440
The female human pelvis has already stretched
to the limits of its structural capacity.

00:15:13.440 --> 00:15:18.400
So the hole in its center is as big as it
can get without compromising the structural

00:15:18.400 --> 00:15:23.310
integrity of the pelvis while still allowing
women to walk and run.

00:15:23.310 --> 00:15:25.400
So how have babies adapted to that?

00:15:25.400 --> 00:15:26.430
Well that’s simple.

00:15:26.430 --> 00:15:30.270
A mammal of our size should have a gestation
period of two years.

00:15:30.270 --> 00:15:32.190
We have a gestation period of nine months.

00:15:32.190 --> 00:15:33.190
Why?

00:15:33.190 --> 00:15:36.080
You gotta get the damned baby out before its
head gets too big.

00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:37.150
What does that mean?

00:15:37.150 --> 00:15:38.930
Well, means it’s vulnerable, right?

00:15:38.930 --> 00:15:43.560
Nothing more vulnerable than a baby human
being except maybe a baby kangaroo, right?

00:15:43.560 --> 00:15:45.870
But it’s got a pouch to hide in at least.

00:15:45.870 --> 00:15:47.920
So we’re born vulnerable, right?

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:49.810
Characteristic of the birth of the hero.

00:15:49.810 --> 00:15:51.610
Who suffers in childbirth?

00:15:51.610 --> 00:15:52.610
Women.

00:15:52.610 --> 00:15:53.610
Why?

00:15:53.610 --> 00:15:55.450
Baby skulls just a little bit too big.

00:15:55.450 --> 00:15:58.640
Has to be crunched and compacted during birth,
right?

00:15:58.640 --> 00:16:02.730
The skull bones aren’t joined together so
that the baby’s head can be squashed and

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:05.690
visibly deformed during the process of birth.

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:09.610
Prior to the twentieth century, what was the
death rate among women giving birth?

00:16:09.610 --> 00:16:10.610
One in three?

00:16:10.610 --> 00:16:11.970
One in five?

00:16:11.970 --> 00:16:12.970
Terrible.

00:16:12.970 --> 00:16:13.970
Why?

00:16:13.970 --> 00:16:16.370
That’s the price you pay for self consciousness.

00:16:16.370 --> 00:16:21.400
"And thy desire shall be to thy husband and
he shall rule over thee."

00:16:21.400 --> 00:16:23.029
This is not an injunction.

00:16:23.029 --> 00:16:26.690
This is a description.

00:16:26.690 --> 00:16:31.779
The additional burden that dependent offspring
place on women, place them at a disadvantage.

00:16:31.779 --> 00:16:34.910
What’s the consequence of that from a historical
perspective?

00:16:34.910 --> 00:16:38.350
Well, any feminist can answer that question
right.

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:45.529
"And unto Adam, he said, because you listen
to your wife, and have eaten the tree, of

00:16:45.529 --> 00:16:49.450
which I commanded thee saying don’t eat
that, cursed is the ground for thy sake.

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:52.050
In sorrow shall thou eat of it for all the
days of thy life."

00:16:52.050 --> 00:16:53.540
Fair enough, right?

00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:56.200
Once you’re self-conscious you work.

00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:57.200
Why?

00:16:57.200 --> 00:16:58.200
Well animals don’t work.

00:16:58.200 --> 00:16:59.200
Why do people work?

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:01.060
Well, because we know, right?

00:17:01.060 --> 00:17:03.080
We know that if it isn’t going to happen
today, it’s going to happen tomorrow.

00:17:03.080 --> 00:17:07.630
And if it isn’t going to happen tomorrow,
well it’s going to happen next week or the

00:17:07.630 --> 00:17:10.140
week after or the month after the year after.

00:17:10.140 --> 00:17:12.150
And we bloody well better prepare.

00:17:12.150 --> 00:17:14.980
So that’s what we do, constantly.

00:17:14.980 --> 00:17:16.860
Prepare and prepare and prepare.

00:17:16.860 --> 00:17:21.699
So we’re not bounded and motivated by what’s
happening from second to second.

00:17:21.699 --> 00:17:24.360
Like the animal is in its still paradisal
state.

00:17:24.360 --> 00:17:29.170
We’re constantly tormented by an endless
string of what if questions because when we

00:17:29.170 --> 00:17:34.950
look at the unknown, we can see the possibility
for everything including our own punishment,

00:17:34.950 --> 00:17:41.090
our own torment, our own demise and so we’re
motivated like no other animal to work.

00:17:41.090 --> 00:17:42.110
And so we work.

00:17:42.110 --> 00:17:46.590
But that is another aspect that alienates
from paradisal being.

00:17:46.590 --> 00:17:51.390
"Thorn and thistles shall it bring forth for
thee and now shall eat the herb of the field,

00:17:51.390 --> 00:17:55.680
in the sweat of thy face shalt thou eat bread
till thou return unto the ground, for dust

00:17:55.680 --> 00:17:58.610
thou art and unto dust shalt thou return.

00:17:58.610 --> 00:17:59.770
Right.

00:17:59.770 --> 00:18:03.740
Therefore the Lord God sent Him forth from
the Garden of Eden to till the ground from

00:18:03.740 --> 00:18:05.620
whence he was taken.

00:18:05.620 --> 00:18:09.390
So he drove out the man and he placed to the
east of the Garden of Eden cherubims and a

00:18:09.390 --> 00:18:13.809
flaming sword which turned every way to keep
the way of the Tree of Life."

00:18:13.809 --> 00:18:22.040
Adam and Eve, right?

00:18:22.040 --> 00:18:24.020
The Mother and Father of all humanity.

00:18:24.020 --> 00:18:28.751
So you can give them a mythological slant
and you can say Adam is culture, say and Eve

00:18:28.751 --> 00:18:31.270
is nature because they’re the archetypal
parents.

00:18:31.270 --> 00:18:33.490
It’s a perfectly reasonable interpretation.

00:18:33.490 --> 00:18:37.020
They have twin sons, Cain and Abel.

00:18:37.020 --> 00:18:43.620
So let’s read first born creatures, first
born human creatures in the new self conscious

00:18:43.620 --> 00:18:44.620
world.

00:18:44.620 --> 00:18:49.850
So what are the first two individuals in the
new self-conscious world like and let’s

00:18:49.850 --> 00:18:50.850
find out.

00:18:50.850 --> 00:18:55.210
"And Adam knew Eve his wife and she conceived
and bearer of Cain and said, I have gotten

00:18:55.210 --> 00:18:57.250
a man from the Lord.

00:18:57.250 --> 00:19:00.520
And again she beared his brother Abel, the
younger brother.

00:19:00.520 --> 00:19:03.910
And Abel was a keeper of sheep but Cain was
a tiller of the ground.

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:08.300
And in the process at time it came to pass
that Cain brought of the fruit of the ground

00:19:08.300 --> 00:19:09.850
an offering unto the Lord."

00:19:09.850 --> 00:19:10.850
Okay.

00:19:10.850 --> 00:19:17.160
So, we’re going to remove this from its
- this story - from its entrapment in a particular

00:19:17.160 --> 00:19:20.392
temporal domain and within a temporal culture.

00:19:20.392 --> 00:19:21.500
We’re going to say something like this.

00:19:21.500 --> 00:19:25.059
Well, if you work you make sacrifices right?

00:19:25.059 --> 00:19:26.670
That’s what work’s all about.

00:19:26.670 --> 00:19:31.260
And the reason you make sacrifices is because
you’re offering up to the unknown the fruits

00:19:31.260 --> 00:19:35.840
of your labour in the hope that as a consequence
of your diligent effort, you’re going to

00:19:35.840 --> 00:19:37.940
be favoured, right because otherwise why work?

00:19:37.940 --> 00:19:42.400
The point of working is to transform the transcendent
into something benevolent.

00:19:42.400 --> 00:19:45.810
So you work and you work and you work and
you say, is that sufficient?

00:19:45.810 --> 00:19:49.960
And the answer you get from the transcendent
is the answer.

00:19:49.960 --> 00:19:54.770
Now it’s certainly true that lots of people
work and it doesn’t go all that well, right?

00:19:54.770 --> 00:19:59.040
They make sacrifices and they do what they
think they have to do and their life is one

00:19:59.040 --> 00:20:00.840
string of catastrophes after another.

00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:01.840
All right?

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:02.860
So we have this situation.

00:20:02.860 --> 00:20:07.100
"In the process of time it came to pass that
Cain brought of the fruit of the ground an

00:20:07.100 --> 00:20:08.670
offering unto the Lord.

00:20:08.670 --> 00:20:13.930
And Abel, he also brought of the firstlings
of his flock, and of the fat thereof.

00:20:13.930 --> 00:20:17.240
And the Lord had respect unto Abel and his
offering."

00:20:17.240 --> 00:20:21.250
So what that means is that old Abel, working
away, may have things that are going great

00:20:21.250 --> 00:20:22.310
for him right?

00:20:22.310 --> 00:20:23.310
Fortune smiles on him.

00:20:23.310 --> 00:20:25.020
He’s doing wonderfully.

00:20:25.020 --> 00:20:27.080
He’s got everything he needs.

00:20:27.080 --> 00:20:31.560
Well, okay and he’s scrounging away in the
ground and things aren’t going as well for

00:20:31.560 --> 00:20:32.790
him at all, right?

00:20:32.790 --> 00:20:34.230
Plagues, locusts, you-name-it.

00:20:34.230 --> 00:20:35.890
Farm life isn’t going well.

00:20:35.890 --> 00:20:37.280
So what happens?

00:20:37.280 --> 00:20:42.160
Well, "Cain was very wrath that his countenance
fell."

00:20:42.160 --> 00:20:44.559
Well, precisely right?

00:20:44.559 --> 00:20:51.630
Because if you work diligently towards a certain
end and you don’t get there then your contenance

00:20:51.630 --> 00:20:52.930
fell, falls, right?

00:20:52.930 --> 00:20:56.840
You’re angry, frustrated, disappointed,
hurt, anxious, threatened, ashamed, guilty,

00:20:56.840 --> 00:20:59.850
the whole panoply of negative emotions.

00:20:59.850 --> 00:21:03.520
And that’s fair enough because of course
if you fail, that’s what’s going to be

00:21:03.520 --> 00:21:06.010
the consequence
But then there’s this little twist on it?

00:21:06.010 --> 00:21:07.010
Right?

00:21:07.010 --> 00:21:11.059
This specifically human twist that, that’s
like that kind of moral of the whole story.

00:21:11.059 --> 00:21:17.000
And so you find the Lord saying, “What,
you know, what’s up with you?

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:18.620
Why are you so unhappy?

00:21:18.620 --> 00:21:23.860
If you just got your act together then you’d
be accepted.

00:21:23.860 --> 00:21:27.730
If you really got your act together”
which is a statement something like this,

00:21:27.730 --> 00:21:33.510
if you keep making sacrifices and the same
terrible thing keeps happening, there’s

00:21:33.510 --> 00:21:38.490
always the possibility that you’re just
actually not doing it the right way.

00:21:38.490 --> 00:21:41.870
And if you’d just get yourself straightened
up, tapped together, right?

00:21:41.870 --> 00:21:46.540
And drop the preconceptions that you don’t
really need, and adjust your behaviour accordingly,

00:21:46.540 --> 00:21:48.610
then fortune would smile on you.

00:21:48.610 --> 00:21:51.800
And that’s exactly what the Lord says to
Cain, right?

00:21:51.800 --> 00:21:55.410
You don’t walk around with such a crabby
look on your face.

00:21:55.410 --> 00:22:00.280
If you did, well, you’ll be accepted and
if you don’t do well, sin lies at the door.

00:22:00.280 --> 00:22:01.280
So what does that mean?

00:22:01.280 --> 00:22:06.480
Well, this is a deep motif in ancient Hebrew
thinking.

00:22:06.480 --> 00:22:10.850
If the world isn’t laying itself out in
a manner that you find acceptable, you’re

00:22:10.850 --> 00:22:12.040
faced with a tough choice.

00:22:12.040 --> 00:22:18.350
Either the world is a terrible place, bent
on your destruction or you’re doing something

00:22:18.350 --> 00:22:19.350
wrong.

00:22:19.350 --> 00:22:22.830
And it bloody well better be that you’re
doing something wrong because if the world

00:22:22.830 --> 00:22:29.240
is a terrible place bent on your destruction,
you’ve got absolutely no hope.

00:22:29.240 --> 00:22:36.059
“And Cain talked with Abel his brother and
it came to pass, when they were in the field

00:22:36.059 --> 00:22:39.830
that Cain rose up against Abel his brother
and killed him.

00:22:39.830 --> 00:22:40.830
“
So what does that mean?

00:22:40.830 --> 00:22:42.480
Well, it’s pretty easy.

00:22:42.480 --> 00:22:43.480
It’s simple.

00:22:43.480 --> 00:22:44.480
It means this.

00:22:44.480 --> 00:22:46.950
Well, say things aren’t that well for you?

00:22:46.950 --> 00:22:51.670
And it’s really not because life’s unfair
and everything’s stacked against you.

00:22:51.670 --> 00:22:58.570
It’s because you’re kind of a arrogant,
stubborn, quasi totalitarian, cowardly idiot.

00:22:58.570 --> 00:23:02.370
And as a consequence of that, the world is
turning into something ressembling a wasteland

00:23:02.370 --> 00:23:03.370
around you.

00:23:03.370 --> 00:23:05.050
And you have this auction.

00:23:05.050 --> 00:23:06.050
Change.

00:23:06.050 --> 00:23:07.460
Or continue.

00:23:07.460 --> 00:23:11.330
Oh, you have another option.

00:23:11.330 --> 00:23:12.410
Man look around.

00:23:12.410 --> 00:23:14.940
There’s all those people doing well.

00:23:14.940 --> 00:23:17.250
The world’s a terrible place bent on my
destruction.

00:23:17.250 --> 00:23:22.630
Couldn’t it be just the most interesting
thing if, as things are going to hell for

00:23:22.630 --> 00:23:29.250
me, I could take a long, just for the ride,
some of those successful people who are successful

00:23:29.250 --> 00:23:31.230
just for unfair reasons.

00:23:31.230 --> 00:23:32.350
Anyways, right?

00:23:32.350 --> 00:23:36.760
Instead of using all that negative emotion
as a cue that there’s something about me

00:23:36.760 --> 00:23:44.290
that might need to be transformed, I can say
well why not just eradicate the target of

00:23:44.290 --> 00:23:45.600
my resentment?

00:23:45.600 --> 00:23:46.600
Right?

00:23:46.600 --> 00:23:50.770
Not only because that sort of removes the
problem of comparison but more profoundly

00:23:50.770 --> 00:23:53.900
– and I think sort of again – limitlessly,
profoundly.

00:23:53.900 --> 00:23:59.010
Let’s say you make the decision that the
world’s a terrible place and it’s bent

00:23:59.010 --> 00:24:00.500
on your destruction.

00:24:00.500 --> 00:24:03.200
And then you think well what’s the logical
response to that?

00:24:03.200 --> 00:24:07.890
And then you think something like this.

00:24:07.890 --> 00:24:17.260
Goethe, Faust, Mephistopheles credo.

00:24:17.260 --> 00:24:25.620
“The spirit I that endlessly denies and
rightly too for all that comes to birth is

00:24:25.620 --> 00:24:29.110
fit for overthrow as nothing worth.

00:24:29.110 --> 00:24:35.760
Wherefore the world were better sterilized
thus all that’s here is evil recognized

00:24:35.760 --> 00:24:43.080
is gain to me and downfall, ruin and sin,
the very element I’d prosper in”

00:24:43.080 --> 00:24:49.510
And Goethe draws our attention to this credo,
not once but twice in his writing of Faust

00:24:49.510 --> 00:24:56.710
and has Mephistopheles say right, once again
"go on, to sheer nothing.

00:24:56.710 --> 00:24:59.429
Passed With null made one.

00:24:59.429 --> 00:25:04.540
/ What matters our creative endless toil /when
at a snatch oblivion ends the coil?/ It is

00:25:04.540 --> 00:25:07.790
by gone, how shall this riddle run?

00:25:07.790 --> 00:25:12.049
As good as if things never had begun yet circle
back existence to possess.

00:25:12.049 --> 00:25:15.039
I’d rather have eternal emptiness.

00:25:15.039 --> 00:25:18.460
"
And so then you think about Cain-like figures,

00:25:18.460 --> 00:25:20.100
like Stalin.

00:25:20.100 --> 00:25:23.059
And you think well what exactly was he motivated
by?

00:25:23.059 --> 00:25:27.400
And on the one hand you think well, he was
trying to extend his cultural – dominion,

00:25:27.400 --> 00:25:37.320
plagued by his own self-conscious nuroticism
he wanted to extend the borders of his totalitarian

00:25:37.320 --> 00:25:42.010
certainty to every corner just to not be plagued
by the unknown.

00:25:42.010 --> 00:25:46.161
and you think fair enough, we're all pretty
nervous and a little stability is a pretty

00:25:46.161 --> 00:25:47.450
good thing.

00:25:47.450 --> 00:25:48.450
Why?

00:25:48.450 --> 00:25:54.000
Because they make a fundamental judgment,
which is the judgement of Mephistopheles.

00:25:54.000 --> 00:25:56.750
Look: life is terrible.

00:25:56.750 --> 00:25:57.750
terrible.

00:25:57.750 --> 00:25:58.750
terrible.

00:25:58.750 --> 00:26:05.309
we're self conscious, we get sick, we go insane,
we're going to die, children, innocent children

00:26:05.309 --> 00:26:07.700
suffer everywhere.

00:26:07.700 --> 00:26:13.910
how in the world is it right to let such a
state continue?

00:26:13.910 --> 00:26:19.880
maybe it will be better, all things considered
to just bring the whole thing to an end.

00:26:19.880 --> 00:26:26.860
and then you think again with Eliade that
the reason human societies fall apart is two

00:26:26.860 --> 00:26:32.080
fold, one is that things go from bad to worse
in their own accord right?

00:26:32.080 --> 00:26:33.990
thermodynamic reality.

00:26:33.990 --> 00:26:35.910
pure entropy.

00:26:35.910 --> 00:26:38.980
structured entities decay.

00:26:38.980 --> 00:26:45.679
but then there's a twist, structured entities
constructed by humans are sped in their process

00:26:45.679 --> 00:26:51.590
of decay by the participants of the individuals
within that society who have essentnially

00:26:51.590 --> 00:26:59.790
decided that the game is not worth the price
and that under such conditions the only reasonable

00:26:59.790 --> 00:27:05.799
thing for a self conscious - painfully self
conscious - individual to do is to work as

00:27:05.799 --> 00:27:12.160
hard as he or she possibly can to take the
maximum amount of revenge on the conditions

00:27:12.160 --> 00:27:18.720
of existence and to ensure that the entire
game folds up and that consciousness disapears

00:27:18.720 --> 00:27:47.080
and that being is eradicated.

